---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "About HomeFixWise";
const description =
  "Learn about HomeFixWise, our mission, editorial approach, and commitment to practical home-repair information for U.S. and Canadian homeowners.";
---

<Base {title} {description}>
  <section class="page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT HOMEFIXWISE</p>

    <h1>Practical home-repair guidance for real homeowners.</h1>

    <p>
      HomeFixWise is an independent educational website focused on home repair
      costs, troubleshooting, maintenance, and repair-vs-replace decisions for
      homeowners in the United States and Canada.
    </p>

    <h2>Our mission</h2>

    <p>
      Our goal is to help homeowners understand common home problems before
      they become more expensive. We aim to explain likely causes, cost factors,
      safe homeowner checks, and when professional service is the better choice.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cover</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Heating and HVAC troubleshooting</li>
      <li>Plumbing and water-heater issues</li>
      <li>Basement and moisture problems</li>
      <li>Roofing and exterior repairs</li>
      <li>Electrical repair-cost guidance</li>
      <li>Repair-versus-replacement decisions</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Safety first</h2>

    <p>
      HomeFixWise does not replace professional inspection or licensed trade
      services. Electrical, gas, structural, and other safety-critical work
      should be handled by qualified professionals.
    </p>

    <h2>How we create content</h2>

    <p>
      Articles are written to answer practical homeowner questions clearly and
      are reviewed for usefulness, safety, source quality, and readability.
      Where costs are discussed, figures are treated as estimates because labor,
      materials, location, equipment age, and project complexity can affect the
      final price.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>